{
  "about": "QuickFlow.dropTarget on both phones: what a + dragged out of the shape source and let go at point ties to. elements are bottom to top: id, box (x, y, w, h), and line, locked or hidden when true. It is the topmost shown element under the point (a finger's reach of 4 units either side) that is neither the source nor a line; a locked one counts, since a connector tied to it does not move it, and a line on top is passed over for what lies under it. target is its id, or null over empty space, where the copy goes instead.",
